@startuml health_check
title Health Check & Disconnection — RMI vs. Socket

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

== RMI Health Check ==

participant "ClientHandlerRmi" as CHR
participant "pingExecutor" as PE
participant "VirtualViewRmi\n(client stub)" as STUB
participant "DisconnectionListener\n(ServerRmi)" as DL
participant "MatchManager" as MM

note over CHR
  startHealthCheck() spawns a daemon thread
  that iterates every PING_INTERVAL (2s).
end note

loop every PING_INTERVAL (2s)
    CHR -> PE : submit(clientStub::ping)
    PE -> STUB : ping()  [remote, timeout 3s]
    alt success
        STUB --> PE : return
        CHR -> CHR : failures = 0
    else TimeoutException / ExecutionException
        CHR -> CHR : ping.cancel(true)
        CHR -> CHR : failures++
        alt failures >= MAX_FAILURES (2)
            CHR -> CHR : tryMarkDisconnected()\n  → disconnected = true\n  → messageSender.shutdownNow()\n  → pingExecutor.shutdownNow()
            CHR -> DL : disconnectionListener\n.handleDisconnection(nickname)
            DL -> MM : disconnect(nickname)
        end
    end
end

note over CHR
  handleTransportError() follows the same path
  (tryMarkDisconnected → handleDisconnection)
  if a sendAsync callback throws a RemoteException.
end note

== Socket Health Check ==

participant "ClientHandlerSocket\n(self DisconnectionListener)" as CHS
participant "MatchManager" as MM2

note over CHS
  startHealthCheck() is called by onLogin(),
  spawning a daemon thread that iterates every PING_INTERVAL (2s).
  lastMessageReceivedTime is updated upon every
  readObject() inside the run() loop (including PongMessage).
end note

loop every PING_INTERVAL (2s)
    CHS -> CHS : sendAsync(PingMessage)
    CHS -> CHS : check inactivity\n(now - lastMessageReceivedTime)
    alt inactivity > TIMEOUT_LIMIT (6s)
        CHS -> CHS : handleDisconnection(nickname)\n  → tryMarkDisconnected()\n      → disconnected = true\n      → messageSender.shutdownNow()\n      → closeStreams()
        CHS -> MM2 : matchManager.disconnect(nickname)
    end
end

note over CHS
  Unlike the RMI handler, ClientHandlerSocket implements
  DisconnectionListener itself: there is no separate listener
  object. handleDisconnection() is called directly by the
  health-check thread and, internally, ends with the single
  call to matchManager.disconnect(nickname) shown above.
end note

note over CHS
  An IOException in the readObject() loop of run()
  triggers handleDisconnection() directly,
  handling sudden TCP drops.
end note

@enduml
